    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "which follows from the assumption that the residual errors for the same individual are uncorrelated. Assuming purely additive gene action, $ \\sigma_A^2 = h^2 \\sigma_y^2 $ of the covariance is due to genetic effects, leaving $ (r - h^2) \\sigma_y^2 = \\sigma_P^2 $ as the covariance due to permanent environmental effects.",
      "source_page": 782,
      "printed_page": 762,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter26:p026:b4"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        143.0,
