      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "0900947e5a618bc79626a2ea79e542c45239708e83fe8abbe837c102840fd2e3"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "One approach to estimating breeding values when repeated measures are contained in the data set is to continue to apply the simple animal model (Equation 26.8), with suitable Z to accommodate multiple records, modifying the residual covariance matrix R such that",
