    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ \\mathbf{a}^{T} = (a_{1}, \\cdots, a_{n})^{T} $ and $ \\mathbf{p}^{T} = (p_{1}, \\cdots, p_{n})^{T} $, and each row of the $ nk \\times n $ incidence matrix Z has all zeros except a one at the position corresponding to the individual measured. This model has the resulting covariance matrices",
